<https://data.stratigraphy.org/data/vis/mainBlurb> skos:prefLabel """This chart presents the BGS Geochronology vocabulary (http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Geochronology/Division) laid out on the structure of the International Chronostratigraphic Chart. Numeric ages, names and colours are those published by BGS; they may differ from the current ICS chart where BGS has not yet adopted a revision.

Hierarchy, ordering and GSSP/GSSA ratification are taken from the International Chronostratigraphic Chart (International Commission on Stratigraphy, https://stratigraphy.org/chart), used under CC BY 4.0. A dashed outline marks a unit where BGS has no value for something shown (usually colour), so the ICS value is used.

British regional and NW European series and stages, and Marine Isotope Stages, are shown alongside. Marine Isotope Stages recorded by BGS with a single age are drawn from that age to the next younger stage.

Built from BritishGeologicalSurvey/vocabularies@9b136fe prez/vocabs/Geochronology.ttl (BGS vocabulary version 2026-11-03T11:14:26Z)."""@en .

sdo:license skos:prefLabel "International Chronostratigraphic Chart structure © International Commission on Stratigraphy, CC BY 4.0."@en .

division:A1 a bgsc:ChartUnit,
        skos:Concept ;
    gts:rank <http://resource.geosciml.org/ontology/timescale/rank/Eon> ;
    gts:ratifiedGSSA true ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy geochronology:Division ;
    skos:broader division:A ;
    skos:definition "Hadean is an informal name for the first of the three major intervals of Precambrian time. It is succeeded by the Archean Eon (Geologic Time Scale 2020, fig. 2.1; https://timescalefoundation.org/)."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch ischart:Hadean ;
    skos:inScheme geochronology:Division ;
    skos:notation "A1"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Hadean"@en ;
    time:hasBeginning [ ischart:inMYA 4560.0 ] ;
    time:hasEnd [ ischart:inMYA 4000.0 ] ;
    sh:order 177 ;
    sdo:color "#AE027E" .

division:AA a bgsc:ChartUnit,
        skos:Concept ;
    gts:rank <http://resource.geosciml.org/ontology/timescale/rank/Era> ;
    gts:ratifiedGSSA true ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy geochronology:Division ;
    skos:broader division:AR ;
    skos:definition "Paleoarchean Era is a division of Precambrian geological time. It is the second of the four eras of the Archean Eon. It is preceded by the Eoarchean Era and succeeded by the Mesoarchean Era (Geologic Time Scale 2020, fig. 2.1; https://timescalefoundation.org/)."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch ischart:Paleoarchean ;
    skos:inScheme geochronology:Division ;
    skos:notation "AA"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Paleoarchean"@en ;
    time:hasBeginning [ ischart:inMYA 3600.0 ] ;
    time:hasEnd [ ischart:inMYA 3200.0 ] ;
    sh:order 174 ;
    sdo:color "#F4449F" .

